From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 17:20:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 216/225] rpmsg: sprd_sipc: add raw-smsg DFS control channel to
 pm_sys

The vendor DDR-DVFS driver talks to the pm_sys DFS task over bare smsg
on channel 22 (SMSG_CH_PM_CTRL): SMSG_TYPE_DFS (13) carries the command
in the flag field (DVFS_CMD_ENABLE=0x0300, AUTO_ENABLE=0x0310,
INQ_STATUS=0x050a, ...), replies come back as SMSG_TYPE_DFS_RSP (14).
No shared memory behind it - the 8-byte mailbox message is the whole
protocol.

Add a "dfs" channel type exposing this through debugfs
(/sys/kernel/debug/sprd-sipc-dfs/{send,status}) and wire channel 22
into the pmsys sipc node. This is a probe for whether the pm_sys DFS
task also services the DCDC_CPU1 topdvfs voltage I2C requests that
currently park at STATE_I2C=4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
